# PER-MACHINE artifacts -- deliberately not committed. See README.md "Wiring".
#
# reports/steward_report.json  regenerated in full on every run (~85KB), and
#                              keyed by an absolute local path (`repo_root`).
#                              Its only consumer is the run that just wrote it.
# steward_state.json           the escalation ratchet. Its semantic effect is
#                              SUPPRESSION, so a shared copy would let any run
#                              anywhere silently consume a finding's one
#                              fleet-wide escalation.
# steward_ref_pins.json        D-102's ref pins, keyed by absolute repo path.
#                              A cross-machine copy would compare this box's
#                              refs against another box's checkout.
#
# state/steward_ledger.jsonl IS tracked and that is not inconsistent: it is an
# append-only audit time series, not a suppression-bearing whole-file rewrite.
#
# steward_ledger_pending.jsonl records a ledger append that a commit failure
# stranded, for the NEXT run to retry landing (steward_sweep.py's never-exit-
# dirty contract). It must never be committed: it is a per-run recovery
# scratch file, not audit history -- the record it holds is only ever
# meaningful until the next successful flush, and once flushed it is deleted.
reports/
steward_state.json
steward_ref_pins.json
steward_ledger_pending.jsonl
